# Usage intelligence

Do not build a live Portal Genie database or API integration until there is a demonstrated need.

Initial usage source: **uploaded CSV/XLSX**. Later adapters (scheduled import, API, reporting DB) must produce the same `NormalizedUsageProfile`. Sales intelligence must not depend on the ingestion method.

Do not duplicate the Portal Genie database. Store external IDs, aggregates, lifecycle, scores, trends, and recommended actions only.

Never invent Portal Genie live schema or API endpoints.

Activation thresholds must be configurable. Do not treat interim defaults as permanent until usage is analysed against paying conversion.

Treat accounting-software connection as a major activation signal. Usage fields are product-behaviour evidence, not CRM facts.

If product usage is unknown, do not treat it as low usage. Label it unavailable.

Identity matching is deterministic first. Uncertain matches are flagged for review. AI must not silently merge accounts.
